Requirements from an attached document:
- The document's requirements are the requirements. Do not invent others, and do not replace them with generic ones such as accuracy, latency or robustness.
- When they have IDs (R1, FR-2.1, REQ-3), plan one requirement per ID. Name it "<ID>: <requirement as written>", e.g. "R1: Never diagnoses or implies a likely condition". Its description is the acceptance criteria, quoted as written.
- Do not reword, shorten, merge or split them, and do not re-number them.
- When the user names a subset ("R1-R3", "only R2"), plan exactly those IDs.
- When they have no IDs, keep each requirement's own wording for its name and description.
- A metric checks what the acceptance criteria say, and its name says that too. "Never diagnoses" is checked by a metric like "No Diagnosis Given", never "Diagnostic Accuracy".
